  "identifier": "MATLAB:err_static_workspace_violation",
  "why": "the violation comes from the probe calling run() from inside a function, not from codegen; p56_coder_scripttop.m re-measures the same entry shape at true top level and reaches codegen in both channels"
 },
 "finding": [
  "codegen succeeds in BOTH channels when the entry is given as a file name string: codegen('p56coder_entry','-args',{0.5}) built in a real process (tag A) and through mcpEval/LiveEditorEvaluationHelper (tags B and DIRECT).",
  "codegen fails in BOTH channels with the same identifier and the same empty message, emlc:compilationError, whenever the entry is passed as a function handle -- anonymous (I/K), anonymous with the cell form (O/Q), or a handle to a function that is a resolvable file on the path (P). The console line that precedes it is '无法处理选项' (cannot process options).",
  "the handle-to-a-script-local-function case, re-measured at TRUE top level (p56_coder_scripttop.m, the exact shape Phase 5.5 used), fails the same way in a real batch process and inside the MCP frame: emlc:compilationError, empty message, 0 artifacts, in 7.75 s and 5.49 s. So the entry shape Phase 5.5 blamed the channel for is reproducible without any channel involvement.",
  "the earlier script-local rows (F/L) never reached Coder: they failed with MATLAB:err_static_workspace_violation, which comes from the probe calling run() from inside a function. They are kept but marked superseded, not deleted.",
  "run_matlab_file is not a separate execution channel on this host: its recorded call stack contains the same LiveEditorEvaluationHelper + matlab_mcp/mcpEval frames as evaluate_matlab_code, so 'file vs inline' is a difference of how the code is handed over, not of which process runs it. Tag D built 25 artifacts this way, the same as tag B."
 ],
 "correction": {
  "whatPhase55Said": "artifacts/phase55/coder_session/coder_diagnosis.json and docs/PHASE5_5_AUTONOMY_AND_GAIN_ZH.md section 8 concluded that the discriminating variable is the MCP dynamic-evaluation channel, because a fresh MCP session failed where matlab -batch passed.",
  "whatWasActuallyVaried": "that experiment changed the channel and the entry shape at the same time; its failing case addressed the entry as a handle inside the evaluation frame.",
  "whatThisRoundShows": "with the entry form held fixed, all three ways of running code behave identically: file-name entry builds in batch, in evaluate_matlab_code and in run_matlab_file; handle entry fails in all three. The channel is therefore NOT the discriminating variable; the argument form given to codegen is.",
  "phase55FilesTouched": "none -- the Phase 5.5 record is read-only and was not edited"
 },
 "notClaimed": [
  "the reason codegen rejects the handle forms on this installation is not established. Whether this is unsupported syntax, a version behaviour, or something inside MATLAB Coder's option handling cannot be separated from outside, so no MathWorks internal root cause is asserted.",
  "no official MCP server code was modified, no product was reinstalled, and the user's MATLAB path was not persisted: addpath/rmpath were paired inside each probe and no savepath or restoredefaultpath was run.",
  "Simulink Coder, GPU Coder, coder.compileC and mexCinterface were not probed.",
  "the batch and MCP-file rows are single runs each; no timing claim is made from them, only the pass/fail and identifier."
 ],
 "ruleGoingForward": [
  "codegen assertions run in a real process AND use the file-name entry form; an MCP-reported codegen PASS is treated as unverified until reproduced there",
  "skills must not call codegen with a function handle entry, because on this installation that path yields an empty-message emlc:compilationError with no diagnostic to act on",
  "a harness that wants to compare channels must hold the entry form fixed; changing channel and shape together produced the wrong conclusion in Phase 5.5"
 ]
}